# DEUS Class Map Sprite Standard (v1, draft for Owner approval)

Written 2026-09-26, 16:29–16:50 CT. **0 generations spent** (balance 9,741.1; hard stop 9,740).
Companion files: `DEUS_GENERATION_RECIPES.md` §3.0 (pointer), `PIXELLAB_DOCS_REFERENCE.md`, look-test page `look/LOOK_COMPARISON.html`.

## Summary (for the Owner)
Every playable look is **one PixelLab v3 character per race × class × sex (9 × 12 × 2 = 216)**, drawn in the look of look-test row 6 (the plain v3 human, L09), but at the heights in our repo size chart. Each one is made the same way:
1. A **base** character (8 directions) with idle and walk.
2. Five **States** made from that base: attack, cast, ranged, down, working. Each State gets one animation.

Gear, moods and conditions never change the map sprite. Gear is not shown; moods use emote balloons; conditions use shared overlays; people differ through their 144×144 faceset portraits.

Every prompt is filled from a fixed template. The slots take the chart heights, head/torso/leg pixel counts, anchor points, per-material hex ramps and weapon lengths. Because the look test showed PixelLab treats these numbers as hints, every output is also cropped, anchored and palette-snapped locally, then measured against the chart before it is accepted.

Estimated cost is **~130–150 gens per sprite first pass (~158–183 with retries), ~28,100–32,400 for all 216 (~34,100–39,500 with retries)**. That is 3–4× the current balance, so the Owner needs to decide on budget or the cost options in §9.

---

